  data: {
    LLM: "Memorize your starting two cards. Use Peeks (Queens) to identify your hidden cards or check an opponent's low card. Only swap (Jacks) when you are reasonably sure you are trading a high card for a low one.\n\nWatch which cards opponents draw from the discard pileâ€”this tells you where their low cards are. If an opponent draws a Red King and places it, you know exactly where to aim your next Swap.\n\nThe 'Match' bluff: discard a card quickly to pretend it matches your hidden card. If done correctly, you can shed high cards early. Timing the 'Dacz' call is critical: do it when you have two 0s or Lows and know opponents are still peeking.",
    Player: "Memorize your starting two cards. Use Peeks (Queens) to identify your hidden cards or check an opponent's low card. Only swap (Jacks) when you are reasonably sure you are trading a high card for a low one.\n\nWatch which cards opponents draw from the discard pileâ€”this tells you where their low cards are. If an opponent draws a Red King and places it, you know exactly where to aim your next Swap.\n\nThe 'Match' bluff: discard a card quickly to pretend it matches your hidden card. If done correctly, you can shed high cards early. Timing the 'Dacz' call is critical: do it when you have two 0s or Lows and know opponents are still peeking.",
